WEBVTT

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:15.980
Icchan?

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:17.220
Good job back there.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:20.480
Yeah, you're welcome.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.000
Were they all sold to dairy farms?

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.090
Okay, I see.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:29.710
It's not so easy, after all...

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:34.310
We decided to sell all the horses, too.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:36.970
Gramps said it's too hard on him 
physically to take care of them.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.340
I hope someone nice will buy them.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:46.490
So, I'm going to get a job instead 
of taking over the ranch.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:48.880
Yeah, so...

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:50.320
Icchan, listen.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:53.360
If my family's okay with it,

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.690
would you be interested in 
taking over the Mikage Ranch?

00:00:57.130 --> 00:01:00.040
Your family's been running the 
ranch for generations, right?

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.390
I don't think it's appropriate for a 
brat from a ranch that went bankrupt

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:05.620
to stumble in like it's his lucky break.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.570
Besides, I want my own ranch.

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.300
Yeah, okay.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.630
I understand.

00:01:14.290 --> 00:01:17.000
Sorry. Let's pretend I never asked.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.730
Cheese Processing Room 
 (Biological Production Association: Practicum Room)

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:51.720
<b>Fall Chapter Episode 10
Dream</b>

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:50.190
What?

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.730
Aki, you're going to try 
to get into a university?!

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.310
Yeah, that's where things stand.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.980
Like the University of Agriculture and 
Veterinary Science next door?

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.710
That'd be my top choice.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.570
I liked what I saw when I went with 
the equestrian club to borrow horses.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.780
But that one's tough to get into, right?

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.120
Right, so...

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.620
Hachiken!

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:10.620
I heard you're gonna tutor Mikage?

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:11.830
Y-Yeah.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.390
What, what, what?

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.340
Nice move, you perv!

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.630
Perv-Hachi!

00:03:16.630 --> 00:03:18.490
Shut up, Perv-Chicken!

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.970
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:21.970
Mikage.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:22.990
Yeah?

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.470
Can you show me your recent exams to start?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.350
Huh?

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:30.810
I want to know which subjects 
you're not so good at.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.490
Promise you won't laugh?

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:33.830
Promise.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.960
D-Definitely better than Tokiwa!

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:46.620
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.630
I still think you should take the 
B-track for Japanese History.

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:54.980
You can take entrance exams 
to more universities that way.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:57.220
Japanese History B?

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:00.950
I'm not good at memorizing 
names of historical figures.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.800
My eyes just sort of slide over them.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:06.590
But your scores aren't bad for 
livestock science and crop science.

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:08.350
Crop Science                Livestock Science                Japanese History

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:08.350
You did fine writing down 
complicated cultivar names.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:12.220
But way too many historical 
figures have similar names!

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:13.830
The Taira clan always has 
"mori" in their names!

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:15.480
The Tokugawa clan always has "ie"!

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.570
What's so different about livestock?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.690
<b>Berkshire</b>

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:20.980
There's Berkshire, Hampshire, 
and Yorkshire!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:19.780
<b>Hampshire

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.690
<b>Yorkshire

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:27.570
<i>She probably just isn't 
interested in history.</i>

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.990
<i>I don't want to force it on her 
and make her hate studying...</i>

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:34.250
You should just connect it 
to your favorite topic.

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:38.340
Mikage, do you know about the 
Soma wild horse chase festival?

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.630
Yeah! I do!

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.700
It's in Fukushima!

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:43.400
People dress up as warriors 
and ride horses, right?

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.650
That was started by Taira no Masakado, 
ancestor of the Soma clan.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.160
The tradition is more than 
a thousand years old.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:52.290
Wow! That long!

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.620
Taira no Masakado...

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:55.730
<i>She took the bait!</i>

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.830
And, Masakado's uncle's line eventually 
produced Taira no Kiyomori.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.570
Kiyomori died in 1181,

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:05.520
which is around the time the Taira clan
 went into a losing streak in war.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.350
What was especially amazing

00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:11.020
was when Minamoto no Yoshitsune, 
younger brother of Kiyomori's rival, Yoritomo,

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.090
rushed down a steep ravine on his horse
 and launched a surprise assault

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.750
that crushed the Taira clan!

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.710
Wow!

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.250
The horse and Yoshitsune have amazing skills!

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:23.200
That was the Battle of Ichi-no-Tani in 1184.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:24.650
<i>This is going to work!</i>

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:26.260
<i>Mikage's an easy sell!</i>

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.840
Hey, is Hachiken there?

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.520
What is it, Senpai?

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:34.310
Yo. I want to talk about the pizza oven.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.900
There's talk about making pizza 
baking an official school event.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.070
You should join the planning committee.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.030
Huh? The committee?

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:45.750
You'll join, right? You're a yes-man!

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.360
Um...

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:49.450
I'm sorry, but I can't!

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:50.200
What?!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.800
We were counting on you never saying no!

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.760
Sorry!

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.370
I just can't this time!

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.570
I made a promise to help a friend study.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.040
It's really important for my friend's future,

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.130
so I don't want to cut corners.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:08.470
Well, I guess there's no helping that!

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.400
Value promises with friends.

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.180
Right!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:15.810
Sorry I bugged you when you're busy...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.730
The friend you're helping is a girl?

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:20.480
Yeah.

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.040
It's just the two of you studying?

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:22.830
Yes.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:27.780
Execution.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.990
Pork Bowl!

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:32.370
Hachiken-san, come over here!

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:34.740
Hachiken-kun!

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.370
Sorry.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:38.250
About what?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.630
I'm getting help from you 
in a lot of different ways...

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.090
I feel bad for taking up your time.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.010
Don't worry!

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.250
You know, I like studying.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.380
It's about the only way I can help you.

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:54.350
But really, I'm causing you 
a lot of trouble. Sorry.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:57.230
You've been apologizing 
non-stop since the other day.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:06:59.010
You really shouldn't worry.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:00.440
I'm doing it because I want to.

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:02.650
Right, sorry...

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:03.650
Guestbook 
Please write anything about 
the event you'd like. 
 Equestrian Club

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:04.650
Thank you.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:09.030
Thanks to you, I made progress on my future,

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.240
and with my parents, too.

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:15.780
Thank you.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.170
Aki!

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.040
Let's go to club!

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:24.340
Oh, what's this?

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:25.500
English vocab flip cards.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.880
I figured I should try to learn 
even a little whenever I have time.

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.840
This brings back memories! 
I did this in junior high!

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:35.050
So you really want to take 
university entrance exams.

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:35.850
Yeah.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:40.100
I can't depend on Hachiken-kun 
for everything.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.690
If there's anything I can 
do myself, I should try.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.450
That's love for you.

00:07:45.450 --> 00:07:47.500
Wh-Wh-Wh-What, Sakae-chan?

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.150
Th-Th-That's not how it is!

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:50.000
What?

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.680
You guys aren't going out?

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:53.640
After coming this far, 
you're still on the fence?

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:54.780
Are you an idiot?

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:58.620
<b>Idiot</b>

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.620
Yeah, I'm an idiot. I'm dumb.

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:01.070
What?! You guys aren't dating?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.000
Since you two were studying all 
friendly-like and all... I totally thought...

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:05.790
Ya...

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:09.330
Is that what you'd call "(quasi) happy IRL"?

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.630
<b>(Quasi) 
Happy 
IRL</b>

00:08:14.890 --> 00:08:16.410
Mikage's at the top of her game.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:18.530
She looks like she's having a lot of fun.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:21.650
She must be taking a break with 
these horses from studying.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.650
Let's hope it helps her with both her 
studies and her horseback riding.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:29.360
But history through horses, huh?

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.380
That's an unusual teaching method.

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.250
But piecemeal learning? 
Is that going to work?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.320
I just have to fill the 
gaps between the pieces

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.450
so that she gets the entire history.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.550
Horses are integral to 
the history of humanity!

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.110
At least up until the modern world...

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:47.040
So your enemy is the iron horse...

00:08:48.860 --> 00:08:50.000
Break time!

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:55.800
It's tough to take the national entrance exam
 after going to an agricultural high school.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:58.730
The general subjects are too lax here.

00:08:58.730 --> 00:08:59.640
Yeah.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.880
Oh, didn't your brother 
get into Tokyo University?

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:04.960
Why not ask him for studying tips?

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:09.440
I don't want to ask him for help.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:11.700
Give that stubborn pride to the pigs.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.540
It's for Mikage, right, (Quasi) Happy IRL?

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.500
Don't kick me with manure-caked boots!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.870
And don't insult the pigs!

00:09:19.370 --> 00:09:22.650
B-But I don't know his cell number, anyway!

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:24.370
I do.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.960
He came to do part-time work 
at the farm over the summer,

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.230
so I got his cell number then.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.880
Yo, I was wondering who was calling me!

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:42.640
What's up?

00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.490
Studying to get into a university?

00:09:45.490 --> 00:09:47.600
Oh, I guess I said something like that.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.310
Well...

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:53.060
Can you... tell me how?

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.320
My friend's going to take entrance exams.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.690
What's with the silence?

00:10:00.220 --> 00:10:00.870
Oh...

00:10:01.310 --> 00:10:03.830
Just glad you're coming to me for help!

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.700
I don't even want to ask you for anything—

00:10:06.700 --> 00:10:08.280
I don't know if they'll be useful,

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:11.040
but I kept my notebooks and everything.

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:12.780
They're somewhere back at our parents' place.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:13.840
Go look for 'em.

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:14.740
What?!

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.270
You go get them!

00:10:16.270 --> 00:10:17.710
You go yourself.

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.690
I don't want to see Dad's face.

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:21.260
Hey! Wait!

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.260
Later.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.020
Call Ended

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.020
Call Time

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:28.790
Parents'... place.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:37.740
Hachiken-kun, do you hate 
going back home that much?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.050
You can just dash over and dash back.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:43.790
The dashing's the hard part.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:44.450
Lame!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:48.970
Man, it takes three hours from 
here to Sapporo by train.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:52.680
The stress will eat away at my stomach the whole time.

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.400
Hachiken-kun.

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:54.170
Yes?

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:57.250
Negative thinking will infect the cheese.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:58.400
Get out.

00:10:58.400 --> 00:10:59.550
Really? News to me.

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.470
How to Scrub Raclette Cheese

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.560
Hachiken-kun, you don't 
have to go out of your way.

00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:05.450
No!

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:08.630
My brother's treasure sleeps 
somewhere in that house.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.520
No pain, no gain!

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.130
Let me know if there's anything I can do.

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:14.730
I'll do anything.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:21.660
I mean, you gave me courage 
during my family meeting, right?

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.580
I'd do anything if it'd cheer you up.

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:28.620
M-Mikage!

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:29.330
Yes?!

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:31.910
You should study.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:33.720
These are materials for tomorrow.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.340
Work through them while I'm gone.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:35.920
Okay!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.930
I'm gonna do this! Yeah!

00:11:40.120 --> 00:11:43.440
Do anything... Anything... Any...

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:45.890
Hachiken, you creep!

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.600
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:11:51.660 --> 00:11:52.900
Morning.

00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.640
Sorry, did I wake you?

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.070
You're up early.

00:11:57.070 --> 00:11:58.320
Leaving already?

00:11:58.710 --> 00:12:02.280
I'm gonna take the first train out, 
do the deed, and come straight back.

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:04.430
You sure hate your home, huh?

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.950
It's depressing.

00:12:06.810 --> 00:12:09.090
Oh, thanks for the presents to take home.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:09.900
Sure.

00:12:09.090 --> 00:12:09.900
Yup.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.760
Morning.

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:13.500
Why're you here so early?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.580
<b>Yogurt</b>

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:15.630
What's this?

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:17.540
Homemade yogurt.

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.600
You're going back to your 
family in Sapporo, right?

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:21.300
It'll be gentle on your 
stressed-out stomach, too.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:23.130
Tokiwa...

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.790
Tell me how to make it, too.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:27.500
It's really simple.

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:29.490
You get milk from the farm,

00:12:29.490 --> 00:12:31.390
mix in just a bit of yogurt 
sold on the market,

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:33.390
and let it sit in the bath 
for a couple hours. Done!

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:34.770
Uh-huh.

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:37.400
This bath is used by a lot of people,

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.040
so it's kept at 40 degrees Celsius for hours.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.440
It's the perfect temperature 
for making yogurt.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.460
Uh-huh.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:47.620
Men's bath yogurt...

00:12:48.110 --> 00:12:48.950
Do not want.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:50.590
Why not?!

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:53.480
It's sealed, and if you rinse off 
the outside, there's no problem!

00:12:53.480 --> 00:12:55.460
That's not the problem.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.380
If you made this in the women's bath,

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.540
wouldn't it sell at a
 high price to certain people?

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:01.380
You're a genius!

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:06.800
<b>Limited Express Super Tokachi 2 6:48 Sapporo</b>

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:10.470
<i>I wonder what they put 
in here as presents...</i>

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.470
<b>Presents</b>

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.520
<b>I made 
pickles from 
daikon radish 
-Nishikawa</b>

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.520
Fresh 
Cheese

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.520
<b>I made this 
in practicum, 
try it out. 
-Beppu</b>

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:15.980
<i>It stinks! Why are they all fermented foods?!</i>

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.910
<i>Men's bath yogurt...</i>

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.780
<b>Thanks.</b>

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:24.780
<b>Mikage</b>

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:28.810
Mikage...

00:13:28.810 --> 00:13:34.000
They might object, but I'll 
support you, no matter what!

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.170
That's why I'm here!

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:40.420
Dad, Mom,

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.830
Grandpa, Granny,

00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:44.090
Great-Granny, Uncle...

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.970
I can't carry on the Mikage Ranch.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:51.060
I have a dream!

00:13:53.410 --> 00:13:54.350
What?

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:58.060
Not carrying on our ranch? Why?

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:00.580
I'm sorry. But it's just what I said.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:04.780
I don't intend to... 
carry on the Mikage Ranch.

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.650
Wait, but...

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.030
I thought you went to Ezonoo 
so that you could, right?

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:09.600
Oh!

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:11.130
Don't tell me

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:13.770
you fell in with a bad crowd
 at that city high school!

00:14:13.770 --> 00:14:15.200
Hey, Hachiken-kun!

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.080
Did you do something to Aki?!

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.500
That's not it!

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.930
I want to get a job that'll let me work 
with horses after I graduate high school,

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:23.130
so I won't carry on the ranch!

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.840
That's so sudden...

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.680
We've all assumed that's what you'd do.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.020
It's not sudden.

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:39.720
Mikage was just unable
 to speak up all this time.

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:42.440
I think she was trying to 
send signals in her own way.

00:14:42.820 --> 00:14:46.400
I think she's been holding herself back
 and trying really hard.

00:14:47.270 --> 00:14:50.740
When she talks about horses, 
she's really happy.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:55.390
Can you... notice Mikage more?

00:14:59.610 --> 00:15:01.990
Farmhand, I thought you said you can't speak

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:03.940
as though you understand 
when you're an outsider.

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:04.670
Right!

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.210
I'm sorry! I crossed the line!

00:15:06.740 --> 00:15:12.030
Aki, isn't it cheating to make other 
people say what you want to say?

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:13.470
Say it in your own words.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:19.580
It's not that I don't like our work.

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.550
I have a lot of respect for it, actually.

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:24.440
But I have a greater desire 
to work with horses.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:28.020
Watching Icchan made me think a lot.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:31.160
I don't think I can lie to myself anymore.

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.860
I want to work with horses!

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:36.740
If I can, I want to work behind the 
scenes for Ban'ei horse racing!

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:40.630
Once I graduate from high school, 
can I come work with you, Uncle?

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:41.210
Huh?

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.890
No way! No!

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:46.130
You can't work at the Ban'ei stables
 right out of high school!

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:46.920
Why not?!

00:15:47.430 --> 00:15:48.730
You need a lot of stamina,

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:51.920
and you'll be dealing with huge horses, 
so any injury would be serious!

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:53.230
It's a man's world!

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:55.210
There are women working at the stables, too!

00:15:55.210 --> 00:15:59.390
Sure, but the Ban'ei racing 
industry is struggling!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:02.850
If it goes down, you'd be 
out of a job in no time!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:05.850
You wouldn't suffer if 
you'd carry on the ranch...

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.860
No, she would, because of the debt.

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.390
Oh, don't tell me you're taking this lightly,

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:12.950
thinking you can just take over the ranch

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.480
if you can't get a job in Ban'ei racing.

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:17.700
Even if Ban'ei isn't possible, 
I want to work with horses!

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.830
Bro...

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.930
Can we talk about it like 
it's an actual possibility?

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:24.790
With the assumption that there's an 
open spot at the stables, of course.

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:26.380
P-Pa?!

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:34.890
If you do really want to work in 
Ban'ei racing, there's a condition.

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.340
You have to go to college.

00:16:38.030 --> 00:16:39.200
As you already know,

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:42.330
Ban'ei racing is operating on 
a razor thin margin every year.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:44.890
It's managing because of a devoted fan base,

00:16:44.890 --> 00:16:46.440
but the future is very uncertain.

00:16:46.890 --> 00:16:50.100
Even if I were to take on the 
Mikage family's only daughter,

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:52.580
I can't take responsibility 
if something happens to the industry.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:54.280
If you have a college degree,

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.540
you'll have more options if you need 
to take on another job with horses.

00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:00.020
But going to college costs money!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:02.040
We're already talking about 
how we don't have money—

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:03.660
This isn't about money.

00:17:04.120 --> 00:17:06.220
It's about your future.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.630
But... I'm not that smart.

00:17:11.630 --> 00:17:13.200
That's right, Pa!

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:14.600
Do you know what her grades are like?

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.960
Yeah, I know she's not smart.

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:20.510
We were so relieved she got into Ezonoo 
because of their lax referral system.

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.140
<i>They're seriously making fun of me, 
but I can't say anything back.</i>

00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:25.060
Aki...

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:28.910
If you want to do something you love,

00:17:28.910 --> 00:17:31.860
you have to give what you love a proper study.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.360
You were nurtured by horses, no?

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:39.330
Don't insult them by taking 
on the challenge half-way.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:44.220
Which university would she go to?

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:48.530
Somewhere she can study 
horses... large animals?

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:50.450
Somewhere with the cheapest tuition!

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.710
A public university, then.

00:17:52.140 --> 00:17:54.600
Somewhere she can study horses, and public?

00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:57.580
Ooezo University of Agriculture and 
Veterinary Science immediately comes to mind.

00:17:57.580 --> 00:17:58.220
Yeah.

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.260
You think Aki's smart enough to get in?

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:02.540
Mm...

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:07.740
If she doesn't carry on the ranch <i>and</i> 
 fails to get into college, what then?

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:10.460
I mean, it's pretty much a given 
that she'll fail the exam.

00:18:10.460 --> 00:18:11.510
That's right.

00:18:11.510 --> 00:18:14.190
Jobs won't be easy to find these days!

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.780
Isn't trying to get into that 
one just plain reckless?

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:20.020
A girl with an unremarkable 
education, without a job...

00:18:20.020 --> 00:18:21.910
It's obvious that she'll struggle.

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:24.410
What are we going to do if that happens?

00:18:25.380 --> 00:18:28.120
In that case, um, I...

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:30.460
will take responsibility.

00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:36.230
I'm the one who urged her 
to do what she wants to do.

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.260
So... I'll take responsibility!

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:39.780
Does that mean...

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:40.730
In other words...

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:41.890
You'll marry Aki?

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.840
Absolutely not!

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.030
What?! Whaaat?!

00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.270
No, no, no!

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.350
That's not what I meant!

00:18:49.010 --> 00:18:52.360
I'll oversee her studies so 
that she will get into college!

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.320
Is that not good enough?

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:57.610
Will you still not allow 
Mikage to follow her dream?

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:01.980
But you have your own studies and future 
to think about, too, Hachiken-kun.

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:06.320
Oh, but see, I haven't decided 
what I'm going to do at all yet.

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:09.660
Besides, by figuring out how to 
teach a topic to someone else,

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.460
I might gain a deeper understanding, sorta...

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:14.610
What now, Bro?

00:19:14.610 --> 00:19:15.550
Yeah...

00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:17.490
Aki,

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:20.080
if you were going to carry on the ranch,

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:22.860
I could teach you about this job 
or how to survive in this business,

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:25.550
but if you're going into a different field,
 I can't teach you anything.

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:28.230
I only know farming.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:32.300
All I can do is to figure 
out how to pay your tuition.

00:19:32.300 --> 00:19:34.730
If you're serious about 
your dream, give it a try.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:38.000
Whether you can make your 
dream come true or not,

00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:42.670
do not betray friends who 
support your beliefs.

00:19:47.670 --> 00:19:48.660
Mom...

00:19:49.840 --> 00:19:50.800
Granny...

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:57.540
Sorry...

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.850
Thank you.

00:20:04.070 --> 00:20:05.450
<b>Mikage</b>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:05.450
<b>Thanks.</b>

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:16.070
Thanks to you, I made progress on my 
future, and with my parents, too.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:17.570
Thank you.

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:30.580
Pa.

00:20:30.810 --> 00:20:31.540
Hm?

00:20:31.930 --> 00:20:34.460
How long've you known about 
what Aki was thinking?

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:38.790
When Hachiken was working 
here over the summer,

00:20:38.790 --> 00:20:40.670
the day I came back from the hospital...

00:20:41.430 --> 00:20:44.510
I heard Aki blurt it out to 
Hachiken on the river bank.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:46.920
I see.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:50.640
I guess Aki found a friend she 
can be honest with at Ezonoo.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:00.770
Dad...

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:05.490
I wonder how much they'll all fetch.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.810
I hope we can use the money

00:21:07.810 --> 00:21:10.700
to repay some of the debt 
and send Aki to college!

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:15.830
<i>A frost advisory has been issued again 
this morning in the Tokachi region.</i>

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:17.440
<i>A real winter's coming!</i>

00:21:17.840 --> 00:21:19.520
<i>Please beware of ice on the road.</i>

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:50.220
This story is a work of fiction.
